    "# Motivation: With Great Vol Comes Great Oppourinty\n",
    "## Why are we bothered to look at volatility as an asset class? \n",
    "Firstly, The returns of selling puts, selling insurance effectively has been vastly profitable. As we see below selling put options has been very profitable, there has been a large amount of research to explain these 'puts puzzle' to quote [Bondarenko, O. (2014). Why Are Put Options So Expensive?]. In this paper he gives as one of 3 possible explantions that there is a volaitlity risk premium. Its important to make a disction between the variance and volatitliy, volatilty since it was used in the Black Scholes model has been a popular method of deivation. From 'Trading Volatiltly' By Colin Bennett, the first point in the 'Variance is the key, not volatilty' chapter is that variance takes into account the implied volatiltiy for all strikes with the same expiration. Volaitiltiy and variance have another key disiction also highlighted in Bennett's book, this idea of variance squaring volaitltiy removes all depeandcy on the path of volaitliy. More simply if two assets have the same variance, however, different paths of volaitlty by squaring these changes it removes this. Of course, the different assets will have different higher moments. "
   ]
  },
