    "Bennett highlights the viscious spiral of volaitlity, as if you are the seller of vol you become even shorter vol because of negative vega conveixty. I will do the derivation and explation of this later in an appendix. However, lets ask why were traders selling volatiltiy. They believed it was free money to harvest this insurance investors were willing to pay. This is the volaitlity risk premium, the difference between the implied volaitlity and the realised volatitliy. As preivously, discussed the implied volatiltiy is often larger than the realised causing \n",
    "$$\n",
    "IV \\not = RV\n",
    "$$\n",
    "This leads us to definng our VRP as the difference between Implied volatiltiy and realised volatiltiy, this leads us to our next part PUT LINK HERE. "
